{
  "name": "1 - Embed Knowledge Base",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SETUP — status as of 2026-08-25: already wired, nothing left to configure\n\nThis workflow reads your Airtable \"Knowledge Base\" table (Question, Answer, Category, Active, Embedding Status, Last Embedded At, Embed Error Message) and embeds every Active row into the same Supabase `documents` table Workflow 2 searches at answer time. Run it by hand any time you add or edit FAQ rows.\n\n**Already wired, nothing left to configure:**\n- Airtable base `AI Customer Support Agent` / table `Knowledge Base` — real IDs on every node, not placeholders.\n- Credentials: \"Airtable Personal Access Token (Support Agent)\", \"Google Gemini API\", \"Supabase API (Support Agent Knowledge Base)\" — all attached with real credential IDs, confirmed against the live node config (not just picked by name — see the auto-attach warning in project history if re-wiring this from scratch ever becomes necessary).\n- Supabase: pgvector extension on, `documents` table + `match_documents()` function deployed at **vector(3072)** — confirmed against a real failed insert 2026-08-22 (n8n's own node description claims 768, which is wrong for this model). Rebuild recipe if ever needed: `temp/outputs/supabase-fix-embedding-dimension.sql`.\n\n**Fixed 2026-08-25, full-system audit:** \"Store KB Embedding\" was silently reporting success on real Supabase failures — the same vectorStoreSupabase error-shape bug already fixed in Workflows 2 and 4, just not yet applied here since this workflow had never actually been run. Switched to continueErrorOutput; added a \"Search OK?\" gate after the Airtable read so a search failure stops the run instead of embedding garbage. See node notes below.\n\nThis workflow starts with a Manual Trigger — click the button in n8n to run it.",
        "height": 460,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "sticky_setup_0",
      "name": "Sticky Note - SETUP",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -704
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Wipe Old Vectors First\nDeletes every row in the Supabase `documents` table before anything else runs, so a re-run of this workflow never leaves duplicate or stale vectors sitting next to freshly embedded ones. If the wipe fails, the run stops right here — nothing gets read from Airtable and nothing gets re-embedded until the table is confirmed empty.\n\nRun order is deliberately Wipe → Read → Embed (not Read → Wipe → Embed) so the wipe happens exactly once per run instead of once per FAQ row.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 780,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky_section1_1",
      "name": "Section - 1. Wipe Old Vectors First",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Read Active FAQ Rows\nOnly rows where Active is ticked get read and re-embedded — untick Active on any row you don't want the AI using yet.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "sticky_section2_2",
      "name": "Section - 2. Read Active FAQ Rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        784,
        -160
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Embed One Row at a Time\nOne FAQ row per AI embedding call, never batched. Each row's Question + Answer becomes the searchable text; Category and the Airtable record ID travel along as metadata so a future retrieval can be traced back to its source row. Every row gets its own status written back to Airtable — Embedded or Embed Error — so you can see exactly which rows are actually usable by the live support agent (Workflow 2).",
        "height": 1000,
        "width": 1600,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "sticky_section3_3",
      "name": "Section - 3. Embed One Row at a Time",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1088,
        -368
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "start_embedding_run_4",
      "name": "Start Embedding Run",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "delete",
        "tableId": "documents",
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "id",
              "condition": "gte",
              "keyValue": "0"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "wipe_existing_kb_vectors_5",
      "name": "Wipe Existing KB Vectors",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.supabase",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        288,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000,
      "credentials": {
        "supabaseApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Supabase API"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "notes": "Deletes every row in the 'documents' table so a re-run never leaves duplicate/stale vectors next to fresh ones. The filter (id >= 0) assumes the standard Supabase+LangChain schema (id bigserial primary key) — if your table uses a different primary key type (e.g. uuid), edit this condition to match it. CREDENTIAL: select or create \"Supabase API (Support Agent Knowledge Base)\" here — left with no id on purpose, n8n's API auto-attaches an unrelated existing credential of the same type if one is provided by name only."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ String($json.error ? '' : 'ok') }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "wipe_ok_6",
      "name": "Wipe OK?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.3,
      "position": [
        560,
        0
      ],
      "notes": "True = the delete call came back with no error. False stops the run entirely (see 'Wipe Failed - Run Stopped') so nothing ever gets read from Airtable or re-embedded on top of a table that might still be holding old vectors."
    },
