      "waitBetweenTries": 30000,
      "credentials": {
        "supabaseApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_ME",
          "name": "Supabase API"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "notes": "The 'documents' table, the pgvector extension, and the match_documents() RPC function must already exist in Supabase before this runs. CREDENTIAL: select or create \"Supabase API (Support Agent Knowledge Base)\" here.\n\n2026-08-25: switched to continueErrorOutput. The old setup (continueRegularOutput + a downstream IF checking $json.error) is a confirmed silent-failure bug on this exact node type — vectorStoreSupabase does not populate an error field on failure, so a real insert failure would have been reported as success and the Airtable row marked Embedded when nothing was actually stored. Its two real outputs (0=success, 1=failure) now wire directly to the two Update KB Row nodes."
    },
